			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1775854">
									

<p>This is definitely well-served by the SCP format, I think. The first interview risks being overly expository, but, of course, the entire point of an interview is exposition, and the character herself discusses her ability/need to create and control a narrative (which becomes thematically significant when you consider the actual SCP, which is all about agency). Also, it plays a bit with the usual meta viewer stuff inherent to stories about the circus: We're watching the audience watch the &quot;freak&quot;, but now it's also mediated both by the freak-as-narrator and, of course, by the Foundation and its place in the SCP catalog. This makes me want to tickle this article's tummy, as if it were an adorable kitten.</p>
<p>Upvoted, obviously. Very nice work, dude.</p>

